  - name: "Holy Symbol of Viracocha"
    description: "A gold amulet shaped like a ceremonial knife, the blade the face and headdress of Viracocha and the handle his body. Casts Armor of Ithan, Circle of Protection (Superior; the symbol draws the circle) and Heal Wounds three times a day each, at 10th level proficiency, with no P.P.E. spent. Works only for the priest it was made for. A being with hatred for the pantheon who willingly touches it takes 3D6 M.D.; it cannot be used as a weapon. Repels vampires like a cross."
  - name: "Pantheon Special Powers"
    description: "Also selects three of the special powers listed in Rifts Conversion Book Two: Pantheons of the Megaverse. Without that book, add one more spell per level of experience instead. Chosen with the Game Master."
restrictions:
  - "Spells cannot be learned or purchased; they are acquired only through meditation at each new level of experience."
  - "Cybernetics: none to start; most avoid them, relying on their gods."
side_effects: "BOND OF LOYALTY: the priest''s powers depend on service and loyalty. Betraying the pantheon or the Empire of the Sun, worshipping an alien or evil god, aiding evil supernatural monsters (vampires and demons, not D-bees or non-evil supernatural beings), refusing to help the needy and similar dishonour may lead the god to withdraw his or her support, at the Game Master''s judgement of past service, role-played piety and any current quest. Withdrawal is agonising: for 1D4 hours the priest has one attack per melee, no combat bonuses and all skills at -40%. The defrocked priest loses all powers, bonuses and magic, the holy symbol stops working (and often melts or burns), and the priesthood and the pantheon''s servants know it - exile, abuse and persecution in the Empire follow. A devout character may be readmitted, but starts again at first level."
extraction_notes: "WB9 printed 24-26 (cache p024-p026, page_offset 0). || XP: the Larhold Shaman / Pucara Mind Mage / Sun Priest ladder, printed 192, lower bounds read off a render, stored as given. || GROUP: filed as clergy - the book''s section is Classes of the Empire, with no group heading; the priest''s spells are granted by the gods rather than studied, the rifts-priest precedent. No sdc_base or mdc_base is printed; men_of_arms: false, since it is a priest and not a man of arms (the book says outright they are not trained in the arts of war). || MAGIC: the four gods (ability 3) are a { choose: 1 } of special abilities, each carrying a COMPLETE magic block - the common ladder plus that god''s elemental grants - and the class states no magic block of its own, because a chosen ability''s magic block is used only when the class has none (applyAbilities). A priest who picks no god therefore has no spells; the choice is required by the book, which gives every priest one of the four. Common ladder as printed 25: 6 from levels 1-2 at first, 4 from 1-3 at second, 3 from 1-4 at third, 2 per level up to the character''s level from fourth, written out to 15 (the Mystic''s shape). Common spells are general invocations; no spell_traditions_allowed, so the level-gated picks reach no tradition. Elemental spells are the warlock Air:/Earth:/Fire:/Water: rows (Conversion Book One elemental magic), reached through named spell_lists generated from production 2026-09-25: a *_start list of spell levels 1-2 for the first-level picks, and a full list for later grants, which carry the same level cap as the common spells (levels 2 and 3 capped 1-3 and 1-4, then up to the character''s level). VIRACOCHA: the two-element lock is not enforceable - the list offers all four elements and the note tells the player to hold to the two chosen. PACHAMAMA: ''add one earth spell per level of experience'' is read as one at first level too (seven at first level) and one at every level after; the book does not say eight in all as it does for the other three. INTI grants Globe of Daylight and ILLAPA Thunderclap by name, since both cast them free; the at-will / once-per-minute use is in the ability text. Viracocha''s call for aid, Pachamama''s healing touch and Illapa''s weather sense are prose. || HOLY SYMBOL: the catalog row sun-priest-holy-symbol is starting gear; its three spells are trackable_resources, three per day EACH - the book prints ''three times a day, each at tenth level proficiency'', read as three uses of each spell; the alternative reading, three uses in all, is recorded here. || PANTHEON POWERS: the three special powers from Conversion Book Two are not in the catalog; kept as an ability entry to be settled with the G.M., as is the book''s fallback of one more spell per level. || BONUSES: +2 vs horror factor stored; +1 save vs magic at 3, 6, 9 and 12 as at_level spell_magic (the anti-monster precedent, save vs magic as spell_magic). +1 spell strength at 4, 8 and 12 is in level_progression; not stored as a bonus. || P.P.E. 1D6x10 + P.E., +10 per level, stored as printed. || SKILLS: Quechua is printed as Language and Literacy at 98%; stored as Language: Quechua 98 and Literacy: Native Language 98, both flat (native-tongue convention, per_level 0) - a judgement call, since the catalog has no Literacy: Quechua. Dragonese/Elven +25: Language: Dragonese 50+25, Literacy: Dragonese/Elven 30+25. Two languages of choice +20 as two Language: Other and two Literacy: Other picks. Basic Math 45+20, Demon and Monster Lore is Lore: Demons & Monsters 25+20, Land Navigation 36+10. Hand to Hand: Basic to Expert for one other skill, Martial Arts for two. Related: 8, plus two at 4, 8 and 12. Secondary: ''three secondary skills ... at levels one, five and ten'' read as three at EACH of those levels (the NGR commando precedent for this wording); the one-per-level reading is recorded here. || EQUIPMENT: ceremonial masks have no catalog row and are not stubbed; the energy and archaic weapons of choice are catalog sets. || Cybernetics: restriction text. || WARNING: class-check reports ppe_base and starting_money as fields a racial class would discard - the ordinary O.C.C. case; the book does not say the character stops being its race, so no supersedes_race."
---

## Lore

The priests of the Pantheon of the Sun are the most honoured body in the Inca
Empire: community leaders, looked to by crowds of believers, and now serving
under the direct eye of gods who walk among them. The priesthood includes
administrators and scholars without magic and many clerics with mundane
duties; this class is the itinerant kind, sent to the edges of the Empire and
beyond to heal, protect and fight supernatural threats.

They travel with True Incas, Inca Warriors and other champions, and draw their
power from the bond with their god rather than from martial skill. Some travel
in disguise, especially outside the Empire''s borders, where a priest''s rank can
make enemies.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'inca-sun-priest');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'inca-sun-priest';

